{
  "brush": "brush",
  "rationale": "We built the whole piece around one unresolved teal arc that spirals up out of the lower-left and trails off into open air near the top right, like curiosity itself -- a line that keeps searching instead of closing a shape. In the bottom-left corner, two separate blue strokes converge and then continue on as a single teal line, a quiet nod to Pittsburgh's three rivers meeting at the Point and turning into the visitor's favorite color. Lower right, a small orange figure reaches its arm toward a pink mark, a plain-spoken gesture for a robot built to help a person, while a thin purple loop up top and a few grounding black, brown, and green strokes keep the composition anchored without ever closing off the big teal gesture's room to wander.",
